<title>NORWAY: AKER MARITIME SEES IMPROVED 1997.</title>
<headline>AKER MARITIME SEES IMPROVED 1997.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian offshore supply company Aker Maritime ASA said on Thursday it expected a &quot;sharp increase&quot; in operating profits for 1997 compared with last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Underlying earnings are good, as a result of both positive market developments and improvements implemented within the group,&quot; Aker Maritime said in a statement announcing first-half profits.  </p>
<p>&quot;This year the greatest increase in revenues and profits is expected in the group's UK and U.S. activities as a result of both new contracts and acquisitions, and in Norway, in the areas of products and operations, maintenance and modifications,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
